        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Extract Read Only Query Request"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1781000000002"
          },
          "code": "EXTRACT_READ_ONLY_QUERY_REQUEST",
          "id": "1781000000001",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1781000000001_systemPrompt",
              "name": "systemPrompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": ""
            },
            {
              "id": "1781000000001_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a strict JSON extractor and query classifier for buyer workload requests.\n\nInput Data\nCurrent Procurement BU ID: {{$context.$variables.effectivePrcBUId}}\nCurrent Procurement BU Name: {{$context.$variables.effectivePrcBUName}}\nCurrent User Input: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\nTask\nExtract only the parameters needed to route and answer buyer workload queries.\n\nReturn ONLY valid JSON with this exact shape:\n{\n  \"queryType\": \"lineQuery\",\n  \"mode\": \"count\",\n  \"requisitionNumber\": null,\n  \"lineNumber\": null,\n  \"assigneeName\": null,\n  \"categoryId\": null,\n  \"categoryName\": null,\n  \"deliverToLocation\": null,\n  \"status\": null,\n  \"processingStatus\": null,\n  \"creationDateFrom\": null,\n  \"creationDateTo\": null,\n  \"creationDateLabel\": null,\n  \"businessUnitName\": null,\n  \"groupBy\": null,\n  \"unsupportedReason\": null\n}\n\nQuery type rules:\n- Use \"lineQuery\" only when the user asks for requisition lines, records, or counts with a concrete line-level target or filter. Examples: unassigned lines, unprocessed lines, lines assigned to a buyer, requisition lines in a category, lines for a deliver-to location, requisition/line filters. Only use lineQuery for category requests when the user asks for requisition lines, records, or counts, not workload details.\n- Use \"workloadInsightQuery\" for broad workload questions, app-visible workload insight questions, and outside-scope query handling. Examples: workload overview, workload status, workload health, workload summary, top workload categories, highest workload categories, workload balance, balanced/not balanced category workload, workload details for a category, buyer workload for a category, buyer breakdown for a category, buyers in a category, why a category is not balanced, or requests the workload insight agent should gracefully decline.\n\nMode rules for lineQuery:\n- Use \"count\" for questions like \"how many\", \"count\", \"number of\".\n- Use \"list\" for \"show\", \"list\", \"view\", \"find\", \"search\", \"pull up\", \"get me\" when records are requested.\n\nWorkload insight routing priority:\n- If the user asks a broad workload question without a concrete requisition-line target or filter, route to \"workloadInsightQuery\" even when the user also says show/list/view.\n- If the user says workload details, workload breakdown, buyer workload, buyer breakdown, buyers in, who has workload, balanced/not balanced, or why is a category balanced/not balanced, route to \"workloadInsightQuery\" even when the user also says show/list/view.\n- Route plain \"show/list requisition lines in [category]\" or \"how many lines in [category]\" to \"lineQuery\".\n\nWorkload insight tool guide:\n- Top workload category, category ranking, and workload balance overview questions are answered from GetTop5CategoriesWorkloadSummary.\n- Category drilldown questions are answered by GetBuyerBreakdownByCategoryName using the extracted categoryName.\n- Do not use workloadInsightQuery for simple requisition line count/list questions; those must stay lineQuery.\n- Do not invent counts, categories, buyers, requisitions, or line numbers.\n\nField extraction rules:\n- \"How many lines are unassigned?\" -> queryType = \"lineQuery\", mode = \"count\", status = \"unassigned\".\n- \"List unassigned lines\" -> queryType = \"lineQuery\", mode = \"list\", status = \"unassigned\".\n- \"Show lines assigned to Pat Stock\" -> queryType = \"lineQuery\", mode = \"list\", assigneeName = \"Pat Stock\".\n- \"How many lines assigned to Clare Furey?\" -> queryType = \"lineQuery\", mode = \"count\", assigneeName = \"Clare Furey\".\n- \"Show lines with deliver-to location of V1- New York City\" -> queryType = \"lineQuery\", mode = \"list\", deliverToLocation = \"V1- New York City\".\n- \"How many lines are unprocessed?\" -> queryType = \"lineQuery\", mode = \"count\", processingStatus = \"unprocessed\".\n- \"Show the top workload categories\" -> queryType = \"workloadInsightQuery\".\n- \"Which categories have the most workload?\" -> queryType = \"workloadInsightQuery\".\n- \"Is workload balanced?\" -> queryType = \"workloadInsightQuery\".\n- \"Show workload details for a category\" -> queryType = \"workloadInsightQuery\", categoryName = \"<category name>\".\n- \"Show buyer workload for a category\" -> queryType = \"workloadInsightQuery\", categoryName = \"<category name>\".\n- \"Show buyers in a category\" -> queryType = \"workloadInsightQuery\", categoryName = \"<category name>\".\n- \"Why is a category not balanced?\" -> queryType = \"workloadInsightQuery\", categoryName = \"<category name>\".\n- \"created since yesterday\" -> creationDateFrom = \"now-1d/d\", creationDateTo = \"now\", creationDateLabel = \"created since yesterday\".\n- \"created yesterday\" -> creationDateFrom = \"now-1d/d\", creationDateTo = \"now/d\", creationDateLabel = \"created yesterday\".\n- \"created today\" -> creationDateFrom = \"now/d\", creationDateTo = \"now\", creationDateLabel = \"created today\".\n- \"created in the last 7 days\" -> creationDateFrom = \"now-7d/d\", creationDateTo = \"now\", creationDateLabel = \"created in the last 7 days\".\n- \"Requisition 123\" or \"req 123\" -> requisitionNumber = \"123\".\n- \"Line 5\" -> lineNumber = 5.\n- Set businessUnitName only when the user explicitly names a Procurement BU or business unit, for example \"in the Vision Operations Procurement BU\" or \"for business unit Vision Services\".\n- Do not set businessUnitName for category names, buyer names, supplier names, locations, requisitions, or any value followed by \"category\" or \"categories\".\n\nDo not invent missing values. Use null when absent."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_MULTIRECORD"
              ],
              "enableActions": false,
              "enableCommunications": false,
              "customNotes": ""
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "GenerateInitDisplay"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "GENERATEINITDISPLAY",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1774466376721",
          "id": "1774450316238",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1774450316239_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a specialized UI rendering assistant for Procurement Operations Workload Reporting (Unprocessed Requisition Lines).\n**DIRECTIVE:** Your sole purpose is to transform the provided requisition workload data into a valid `oraInfoDisplay` XML block using the `multiRecordWidget` pattern. The output must be stateless and derived only from the provided input data.\n\n## DATA\nUse the following two sets of data.\nCategory aggregates:\n```{{$context.$nodes.NORMALIZETOP5CATEGORIESRESPONSE.$output.result}}```\nBalanced/Not Balanced data:\n```{{$context.$nodes.DETERMINEBALANCEDNOTBALANCED.$output.result}}```\n\n## INSIGHTS TEXT\n**MUST NOT** generate or include any insights text in the output.\n\n## ROOT CONFIGURATION\n1. `title`: Set to a clear and explicit statement indicating whether the overall workload in the top 5 categories is Balanced or Not Balanced, based on the combined `status` values of these categories. If all top 5 categories have status `Balanced`, the title must be exactly: \"Workload is balanced\". If any category is `Not Balanced`, the title must be exactly: \"Workload needs balancing\".\n2. `description`: **MUST** leave it empty.\n3. `subtitle`: Set to \"Unprocessed requisition lines from the last 15 days\".\n\n## WIDGET CHECK\n- Use `multiRecordWidget`.\n- Only use valid `multiRecordWidget` properties: `cols`, `rows` with `cells` and optional `action`.\n\n## REAL INPUT SHAPE\nEach element in `topCategories[]` has only these fields:\n- `categoryId` (number)\n- `categoryName` (string)\n- `docCount` (number): total unprocessed requisition lines for the category\n- `distinctBuyerCount` (number): number of buyers with requisition lines in the category\n- `buyerLoadStats.min` (number): minimum lines assigned to one buyer\n- `buyerLoadStats.max` (number): maximum lines assigned to one buyer\n- `buyerLoadStats.avg` (number): average lines assigned per buyer, used only by the balance-status data\n\n## STRICT MAPPING RULES\nDefine columns in this exact order:\n1. \"Categories with Highest Volume\" - map from `categoryName`\n2. \"Workload\" - render as a badge. Badge text must be exactly `Balanced` or `Not Balanced`. Badge `priority` must be `success` for `Balanced` and `alert` for `Not Balanced`. Set the value only from each category's `status` in the Balanced/Not Balanced data.\n3. \"Requisition Lines\" - map from `docCount`\n4. \"Buyers\" with `showOnExpand=\"true\"` - map from `distinctBuyerCount`; if missing, use \"���\".\n5. \"Minimum Lines Assigned to Buyer\" with `showOnExpand=\"true\"` - map from `buyerLoadStats.min`; if missing, use \"���\".\n6. \"Maximum Lines Assigned to Buyer\" with `showOnExpand=\"true\"` - map from `buyerLoadStats.max`; if missing, use \"���\".\n\n## ROW CONSTRUCTION\n- `multiRecordWidget.rows`: one row per `topCategories[]` record.\n- Sort rows by `docCount` descending.\n- Each row's `cells` must contain exactly 6 values in the same order as `cols`.\n\n## ACTION LOGIC\n- Include an `action` property on each row.\n- Use `ora.Invoke(\"ViewBuyersBreakdown\", \"ViewBuyersBreakdown:{\\\"CategoryId\\\":categoryId, \\\"CategoryName\\\":categoryName, \\\"Workload\\\": status}\" )`.\n- The second argument of `ora.Invoke` must start with `ViewBuyersBreakdown:` followed by the JSON payload containing `CategoryId`, `CategoryName`, and `Workload`.\n\n## OUTPUT REQUIREMENT\nProduce a single `oraInfoDisplay` XML block containing:\n- The root `oraInfoDisplay` element with `title`, `description`, and `subtitle`.\n- One `multiRecordWidget` with the `cols` and `rows` constructed from `topCategories`."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "GenerateSummary"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "GENERATESUMMARY",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1774466405019",
          "id": "1774462429243",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1774462429244_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a concise procurement workload summary assistant.\n\nDATA:\n{{$context.$nodes.NORMALIZETOP5CATEGORIESRESPONSE.$output.result}}\n\nTASK:\nReturn one concise, plain-text summary line.\n\nNO-DATA RULE:\nIf topCategories is missing, null, not an array, or an empty array, return exactly:\nNo unprocessed requisition lines were found in buyer queues for the last 15 days. No workload balancing action is needed\n\nDATA RULE:\nIf topCategories has records, identify the single most important insight from the data.\n\nUse only these fields:\n- categoryName: category name\n- docCount: number of requisition lines\n- distinctBuyerCount: number of buyers with requisition lines in the category\n- buyerLoadStats.min: minimum number of requisition lines assigned to one buyer\n- buyerLoadStats.max: maximum number of requisition lines assigned to one buyer\n\nRULES:\n- Do not invent categories, counts, buyers, or workload patterns.\n- Return only one concise sentence."
            },
            {
              "id": "1774462429243_systemPrompt",
              "name": "systemPrompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": ""
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "description": "Parses the extractor output and normalizes reassignment parameters.",
            "name": "Normalize Reassignment Request",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "const raw = $context.$nodes.EXTRACT_REASSIGNMENT_REQUEST?.$output;\nlet parsed = raw;\n\nif (raw && typeof raw === \"object\" && raw.result !== undefined) {\n  parsed = raw.result;\n}\n\nif (typeof parsed === \"string\") {\n  const trimmed = parsed.trim().replace(/^\\`\\`\\`json\\s*/i, \"\").replace(/^\\`\\`\\`\\s*/i, \"\").replace(/\\`\\`\\`$/i, \"\").trim();\n  try {\n    parsed = JSON.parse(trimmed);\n  } catch (error) {\n    const match = trimmed.match(/\\{[\\s\\S]*\\}/);\n    parsed = match ? JSON.parse(match[0]) : {};\n  }\n}\n\nparsed = parsed && typeof parsed === \"object\" ? parsed : {};\n\nconst message = String($context.$system?.$inputMessage || $context.$triggers?.REST?.$input?.message || \"\");\nconst normalizedMessage = message.toLowerCase();\nconst procurementBUId = $context.$variables.effectivePrcBUId ?? null;\nconst procurementBUName = $context.$variables.effectivePrcBUName ?? null;\n\nfunction compact(value) {\n  return value === null || value === undefined ? null : String(value).trim() || null;\n}\n\nfunction titleCaseName(value) {\n  const text = compact(value);\n  if (!text) return null;\n  return text.replace(/\\s+/g, ' ').replace(/\\b[A-Za-z]/g, c => c.toUpperCase());\n}\n\nfunction inferFromToBuyers() {\n  const matches = Array.from(message.matchAll(/\\bfrom\\s+([A-Za-z][A-Za-z .'-]*?)\\s+to\\s+([A-Za-z][A-Za-z .'-]*?)(?:[.!?]|$)/gi));\n  if (!matches.length) return {};\n  const match = matches[matches.length - 1];\n  return {\n    sourceBuyerName: titleCaseName(match[1]),\n    assigneeName: titleCaseName(match[2])\n  };\n}\n\nconst inferredBuyers = inferFromToBuyers();\n\nconst extracted = {\n  requisitionNumber: parsed.requisitionNumber != null ? String(parsed.requisitionNumber).trim() : null,\n  lineNumber: parsed.lineNumber != null ? Number(parsed.lineNumber) : null,\n  assigneeName: compact(parsed.assigneeName) || inferredBuyers.assigneeName || null,\n  sourceBuyerName: compact(parsed.sourceBuyerName) || inferredBuyers.sourceBuyerName || null,\n  categoryName: parsed.categoryName != null ? String(parsed.categoryName).trim() : null,\n  deliverToLocation: parsed.deliverToLocation != null ? String(parsed.deliverToLocation).trim() : null,\n  status: parsed.status != null ? String(parsed.status).trim().toLowerCase() : null,\n  scope: parsed.scope != null ? String(parsed.scope).trim().toLowerCase() : null,\n  procurementBUId,\n  procurementBUName,\n  originalMessage: message\n};\n\nif (!extracted.status && /\\bunassigned\\b/.test(normalizedMessage)) {\n  extracted.status = \"unassigned\";\n}\n\nif (!extracted.scope) {\n  extracted.scope = extracted.requisitionNumber ? (extracted.lineNumber != null ? \"line\" : \"requisition\") : \"bulk\";\n}\n\nreturn extracted;"
          },
