              "id": "1778000000003_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "## DATA\nWorkload preview data:\n{{$context.$nodes.DIRECT_CALCULATE_TARGET_BUYER_PREVIEW.$output.result}}\nPrepared reassignment payload:\n{{$context.$nodes.PREPARE_REASSIGNMENT_PAYLOAD.$output.result}}\nBuyer ID to Buyer Name mapping:\n{{$context.$nodes.DIRECT_EXTRACTBUYERIDNAMEMAPPING.$output}}\n\n## TASK\nGenerate exactly two widgets in the required output format.\n\n### FIRST WIDGET\nGenerate a multirecord widget that previews the reassignment impact for the source and target buyers when both are present.\n\nThe first widget columns must be exactly:\n- Buyer\n- Requisition Lines Before Reassignment\n- Requisition Lines After Reassignment\n\nUse the workload preview data exactly. If the data contains both source and target buyer rows, include both rows in the same order as provided.\n\n### SECOND WIDGET\nGenerate a record widget that captures the reason and submits the reassignment:\n- oraFormSubmit id: \"reassignment_reason_form\"\n- readOnly: false\n- no title\n- no description\n- include a submit button labeled \"Submit\"\n\nFields:\n1. textarea field\n   - id: \"reassignment_reason\"\n   - label: \"Reason (required, 240-character limit)\"\n   - value: \"Reassigned for workload balancing\"\n\n2. system field\n   - id: \"reassignment_payloads\"\n   - value: \"__REASSIGNMENT_PAYLOAD__\"\n\n3. system field\n   - id: \"buyerIdNameMapping\"\n   - value: \"__BUYER_ID_NAME_MAPPING__\"\n\n## RULES\n- Return only the two widgets.\n- Do not add explanations.\n- Preserve ids exactly as given.\n- Use \"__REASSIGNMENT_PAYLOAD__\" exactly as the system field value.\n- Use \"__BUYER_ID_NAME_MAPPING__\" exactly as the system field value."
